# Git remotes — GitHub primary, iConnectPlus mirrors, GitLab on demand

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Role |
|--------|-----|------|
| `origin` | `https://github.com/ronanop/enterprise-erp.git` | **Primary** — fetch + default push |
| `iconnectplus` | `https://github.com/Moksh-CacheDigitech/iConnectPlus.git` | **Always-synced mirror** of origin |
| `iconnectplus-erp` | `https://github.com/moksh-sharma/iConnectPlus-ERP.git` | **Always-synced mirror** of origin (code only) |
| `gitlab` | `https://172.16.200.77/cachedigitech/cache-erp-vapt-31-aug.git` | Mirror — update only on explicit request |

GitHub `origin` is the source of truth. Both `iconnectplus` and `iconnectplus-erp` must stay matched to origin on every push.

Local `origin` is configured with **three push URLs** (primary + both iConnectPlus mirrors), so `git push origin …` updates all three. The named `iconnectplus` and `iconnectplus-erp` remotes remain available for explicit sync.

**`iconnectplus-erp` sync scope:** git refs / code only. Do **not** sync collaborators, teams, webhooks, or other GitHub repo settings from origin onto this mirror. Keep collaborators cleared on that repo unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.

## When the user asks to push / push to git

1. Push to **origin** (this also syncs both iConnectPlus mirrors via extra push URLs).
2. If dual/triple push URLs are missing or a mirror did not update, also push the same ref to `iconnectplus` and/or `iconnectplus-erp`.
3. Do **not** push or sync GitLab unless they also asked to sync GitLab.

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
# Fallback if a mirror did not update with origin:
git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>
git push iconnectplus-erp HEAD:<branch>
```

## When the user asks to sync iconnectplus / iconnectplus-erp / keep iConnectPlus synced

1. Ensure local matches what should be on origin (push to `origin` first if needed).
2. Push the same refs to `iconnectplus` and/or `iconnectplus-erp` as requested (or both when they said keep iConnectPlus synced).

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>
git push iconnectplus-erp HEAD:<branch>
```

## When the user asks to sync gitlab

1. Ensure local branch matches what should be on GitHub (push to `origin` first if there are unpushed commits).
2. Push the same refs to GitLab so it matches GitHub.

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push gitlab HEAD:<branch> --force-with-lease
```

Prefer matching the current branch name on both remotes. Use `--force-with-lease` only when histories diverged and the user intends the source remote to overwrite the target.

This GitLab host uses a self-signed cert. Local repo already has `http.https://172.16.200.77/.sslVerify=false`. Auth requires a GitLab username + PAT (or SSH key); do not prompt for passwords in non-interactive sessions — ask the user for a token/URL with credentials if push fails.

## Do not

- Skip syncing `iconnectplus` or `iconnectplus-erp` when pushing to origin / "push to git"
- Sync collaborators / GitHub settings onto `iconnectplus-erp` (code-only mirror)
- Auto-sync GitLab on every GitHub push
- Treat GitLab or either iConnectPlus mirror as primary fetch when the user said "push to git"
- Sync the other direction (GitLab → GitHub, or mirrors → origin) unless the user explicitly asks
